# Binding: no tool calling (an eval's, t3-install o1_binding_without_tool_calling)

This install's model with `tool_calling` false: a binding no profile that offers tools can wear. The O1 case runs
under it (`binding:`, `evals.py`'s standins runner) and is refused by name before any plan or card. The router's
own call still goes to the model named here, so it is the install's model.

```json
{
  "stew": "2026-11-08-draft",
  "kind": "binding",
  "name": "eval-no-tool-calling",
  "api": "ollama",
  "endpoint": "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
  "model": "steward:1",
  "provides": {
    "tool_calling": false,
    "context": 65536,
    "structured_output": true,
    "reasoning_effort": true
  },
  "hardware": "one 16 GB GPU",
  "options": {
    "num_ctx": 65536,
    "keep_alive": "30m"
  }
}
```
